                <pb facs="0953" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–1948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-12-19">December 19, 1948</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        19—8:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>CAT plane took off approximately 4:40 p.m. this afternoon from Tientsin
                    Changkueichuang field under Communist small arms fire. Field now unsafe for
                    further flights. Only two CAT American employees able to board departing
                    plane.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
